 "review": {
  "score": 7.0,
  "round": 1,
  "problems": [
   "At a glance the fork is too weak. The graph-coloured U-curve sits almost entirely behind the disc and, against the charcoal ground, its visible arms look like a dark shadow or halo rather than a charcoal fork holding the mirror. The swivel mount, which the spec calls for, barely shows.",
   "The pale grey glass with a single glint could read as a porthole, a clock face or a magnifying glass. It needs a little more mirror reflection to read as a relay mirror for light beams.",
   "The two champ rivets at (0,-235) and (0,-125) have no sway anim, but the disc they sit on does sway. That makes them drift about 3px off the frame during the motion.",
   "The base plate is small and flat for a 2.4-tall prop on a thin post. It reads slightly top-heavy next to the person, though the scale against the person is fine (the mirror centre is at about head height)."
  ]
 },
 "for": "Free-standing round brass-framed relay mirror on a swivel post. Mirrors bounce a light beam from one end of the island to the other, so the film can show it cro",
 "source": "minted",
 "created": "2026-11-05",
