 "sprite_review": {
  "score": 6.0,
  "problems": [
   "At a glance it reads as a Victorian vanity or shaving mirror on a stand, not a relay mirror for bouncing light. The ornate cast-iron column, the claw-foot flare at the base and the thin decorative rim all point to a dressing table.",
   "It is too small next to the person. The spec says h 2.4, which is taller than the figure, but in the scene the top of the glass only reaches about the man's shoulder.",
   "The frame is mostly dark iron with only a thin gold edge. The spec asks for a round brass-framed mirror, so the brass should be the main colour of the frame.",
   "The fork is a thin ring that hugs the frame and is hard to make out. The pivot bolts at each side are tiny, so the swivel idea doesn't read.",
   "Nothing shows it is optical or aimable. There is no visible swivel joint where the post meets the fork."
  ]
 }
}